# https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing
Fencing Sphere	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBaseSphere.Fencing	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_COMBAT_TALENTS,1	DEFINE:SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|0	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DEFINE:SPHERES_FENCING_FOOTWORK_COUNT|0	DEFINE:SPHERES_BAB_FENCING|BAB	DEFINE:SPHERES_DC_FENCING|10+floor(SPHERES_BAB_FENCING/2)+SPHERES_PRACTITIONER_MOD	BONUS:SKILLRANK|Bluff|min(TL,5*SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS)|TYPE=SpheresTraining	DEFINE:SPHERES_FATAL_THRUST_DICE|1+floor(SPHERES_BAB_FENCING/5)	DESC:Fencers are quick fighters who use nimble footwork and expert feints to open up their target before landing a fatal blow. When you gain the Fencing sphere, you gain 5 ranks in the Bluff skill, plus 5 ranks per additional talent spent in the Fencing sphere [maximum ranks equal to your total Hit Dice]. If you already have ranks in the Bluff skill you may immediately retrain them, but you do not get to retrain when only temporarily gaining talents, such as through the armiger’s customized weapons class feature. Fatal Thrust: Whenever you make an attack action or an attack of opportunity against a target that is within 30 ft. and that you are flanking, that is flat-footed, or that has lost its Dexterity bonus to AC [such as through a successful feint], you deal an additional +1d6 precision damage to the target. This damage is not multiplied on a critical hit. This damage increases by an additional 1d6 precision damage for every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess. A fencer may apply the effects of a single [exploit] talent to any fatal thrust. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing
Fencing - Darting Crane	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:While in this stance, whenever a creature within reach misses you with a melee attack, you may expend an attack of opportunity to perform a feint against that creature as a free action that can be taken outside of your normal turn. You may not use this talent in conjunction with [deflect] talents or any other ability that would grant you an attack or combat maneuver due to a missed attack against you. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc2
Fencing - Death From Afar	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You may use fatal thrust on a ranged attack action out to your first range increment. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc3
Fencing - Expert Feint	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When you succeed at a feint check against a target, that target also loses its Dexterity bonus to its armor class against all attacks until the beginning of your next turn, in addition to your next attack. Associated Feat: Greater Feint. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc4
Fencing - Expert Fence	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:As a swift action, you may choose one edge of your space and create a metaphorical fence for 1 round. That edge is treated as partial cover for attacks targeting you only. At +10 base attack bonus, you may expend martial focus to reduce this to an immediate action. Partial cover provided by this talent does not block line of effect and cannot be used to attempt a Stealth check. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc5
Fencing - Exploitative Strike	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Source: Arcforge Players Compendium As long as you have martial focus, you may make a fatal thrust against a creature who is dazzled or who is suffering Perception penalties from the deafened condition. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc6
Fencing - Fast Feint	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You may attempt to feint a creature as a move action. In addition, once per round when you succeed on a feint attempt against a creature, you may expend martial focus to move up to your speed. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity from the target of your feint. Associated Feat: Improved Feint. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc7
Fencing - Fatal Opening	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Whenever you attack a target that has lost its Dexterity bonus to its armor class due to your successful feint, your critical threat range for that attack is doubled. If you possess the Expert Feint talent, this doubling applies to all attacks against the target while it is suffering the effects of your feint. This does not stack with other effects that extend the threat range of a weapon. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc8
Fencing - Feint Strike	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Whenever you succeed at a feint against a creature, you may make a single attack against them with any weapon you are wielding as a swift action. You may expend your martial focus to instead make this attack as an attack of opportunity. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc9
Fencing - Focusing Feint	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Whenever you succeed at a feint against a creature, you may regain your martial focus as a swift action. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc10
Fencing - Footwork	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_FOOTWORK_COUNT|1	PREVARLT:SPHERES_FENCING_FOOTWORK_COUNT,2	DESC:As long as you have martial focus, you may make a 5-foot step as an immediate action. If this movement is done in response to an attack made against you, you gain an extra +2 dodge bonus to your AC and CMD against that attack. If you take this step, you cannot take a 5-foot step during your next turn. If you take an action to move during your next turn, subtract 5 ft. from your total movement. You may take this talent twice. If taken twice, you may move up to 10 ft. when you take this immediate action. You may still take a 5-foot step during your next turn, and any movement you make using this talent does not subtract any distance from your movement during your next turn. Associated Feats: Step Up, Following Step if taken twice. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc11
Fencing - Group Cover	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Your quick movements allow you to temporarily use one enemy as cover against another enemy. As long as you have martial focus, every enemy that threatens you suffers a -2 penalty to their attack rolls against you for every other creature adjacent to them that also threatens you. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc12
Fencing - Impassable Defense	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When you take the total defense action, you still may make attacks of opportunity. If you possess the Lunge talent, you may increase your threatened area by 5 ft. when determining the range at which you may make attacks of opportunity while using the total defense action, but suffer a -2 penalty to attacks made at this extended range, as detailed under the Lunge talent. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc13
Fencing - Isolating Repartee	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When you are the only creature within 10 feet of a target which the target perceives, that target takes a penalty on Bluff, Diplomacy, Intimidate, and Perform checks equal to your practitioner modifier. If you possess at least 10 ranks in either Bluff or Sense Motive, this penalty increases to twice your practitioner modifier. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc14
Fencing - Lucky Thrust	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Source: Baron’s Glorious Arena Whenever you confirm a critical hit from an attack action or attack of opportunity against a creature within range of your fatal thrust, you may add your fatal thrust damage to the attack even if the attack would not normally add fatal thrust damage. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc15
Fencing - Lunge	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:As long as you have martial focus, you may increase the range at which you may make melee attacks by 5 ft., but suffer a -2 penalty to attack rolls made against targets within this extended range. This does not affect your threatened area, only the reach of your attacks, and does not stack with other, similar effects. Associated Feat: Lunge. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc16
Fencing - Masterful Defense	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Whenever you fight defensively, you only suffer a -2 penalty to attack rather than the usual -4. In addition, you gain an additional +1 dodge bonus whenever you fight defensively or take the total defense action. Associated Feat: Crane Style. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc17
Fencing - Open Guard	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Whenever you feint a target, that target is battered for 1 round. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc18
Fencing - Pace Setter	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Whenever you deal your Fencing sphere precision damage to a target, you can force the creature to move 5 ft. in any direction as long as this would not cause them to end their movement in dangerous terrain. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc19
Fencing - Parry And Riposte	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When a creature makes a melee attack against you, you may expend your martial focus and use an attack of opportunity to attempt to parry that attack. Make an attack roll as if you were making an attack of opportunity, but for each size category the attacking creature is larger than you, you take a –2 penalty on this roll. If your result is greater than the attacking creature’s result, the creature’s attack automatically misses and you regain your martial focus. If your base attack bonus is +5 or greater, you may choose to make a single melee attack against a creature whose attack you have successfully parried instead of regaining your martial focus. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc20
Fencing - Read Foe	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	BONUS:SKILLRANK|Sense Motive|min(TL,5*SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS)|TYPE=SpheresTraining	DESC:You have learned to read the subtle cues of your enemy, and to see through enemy feints. You gain 5 ranks in the Sense Motive skill, plus 5 ranks per additional talent spent in the Fencing sphere [maximum ranks equal to your total Hit Dice]. If you already have ranks in the Sense Motive skill you may immediately retrain them, but you do not get to retrain when only temporarily gaining talents, such as through the armiger’s customized weapons class feature. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc21
Fencing - Skewer	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:When dealing your Fencing sphere precision damage to a creature, you may expend your martial focus to increase the bonus precision damage to become +1d6, +1d6 at +3 base attack bonus and every +2 thereafter. In addition, you may apply two different [exploit] talents to this attack. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc22
Fencing - Substituting Feint	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Source: Diamond Spheres: Hustle & Bustle Whenever you succeed at a feint against a creature, instead of denying them their Dexterity bonus to AC, you can either plant an item on the creature or trick the creature into accepting a one-handed object you are holding [as long as they have a free hand] as a free action. You can outwit the creature as a cost or expend your martial focus to have the creature be denied their Dexterity to AC as normal. Associated Feat: Deceptive Exchange [Ultimate Combat]. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc23
Fencing - Unlikely Feint	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You do not suffer a penalty when feinting against non-humanoids, and the penalty against feinting a creature with an Intelligence of 1 or 2 is reduced to -4. You may attempt to feint mindless creatures, but suffer a -8 penalty. For every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess, these penalties are reduced by 2 [minimum 0]. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc24
Fencing - Verbal Feint	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You may throw people off their guard with simple motions and well-placed words. You do not need a weapon in order to attempt a feint check, and can feint targets within 30 ft. Only targets that can hear you may be targeted with a verbal feint. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc25
Fencing - Ankle Strike	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You may attempt a trip combat maneuver against the target as a free action which does not provoke an attack of opportunity. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc27
Fencing - Arm Strike	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Your attack strikes their arm in a critical spot. The target suffers a -2 penalty to all attack rolls, ability checks, or skill checks made with that arm for 1d4 rounds. For every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess, this penalty lasts for an additional round. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc28
Fencing - Belt Cutter	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You may attempt a steal combat maneuver against the target as a free action which does not provoke an attack of opportunity. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc29
Fencing - Chest Strike	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Your attack strikes the target’s chest. The target must pass a Fortitude save or become sickened for 1d4 rounds. For every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess, this penalty lasts for an additional round. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc30
Fencing - Distracting Blades	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:The target loses the ability to make attacks of opportunity for 1 round. For every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess, this penalty lasts for an additional round. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc31
Fencing - Face Strike	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Your attack cuts into the target’s face, impeding their ability to see and hear. The target treats all targets as if they had partial concealment [a 20 percent miss chance] for 1 round, and suffers a -2 Penalty to all Perception checks. For every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess, this penalty lasts an additional round. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc32
Fencing - Hand Slash	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:Make a disarm combat maneuver against the target as a free action. This disarm does not provoke an attack of opportunity. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc33
Fencing - Leg Slash	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:The target’s movement types are halved for 1d4 rounds. For every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess, this penalty lasts for an additional round. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc34
Fencing - Repositioning Strike	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You cause the target to stumble, letting you slip past them. You may immediately move up to half your movement speed as a free action, so long as you end your movement in a space adjacent to the target, and may even move through the target’s occupied space when doing so. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity from the target. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc35
Fencing - To The Hilt	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:You create a large wound on the target that others can exploit. For 1 round, the target’s damage resistance is reduced by an amount equal to 1/2 your base attack bonus [minimum 1]. For every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess, this penalty lasts for an additional round. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc36
Fencing - Wide Open	CATEGORY:Spheres Combat Talent	TYPE:SpheresBasicTalent.Fencing	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Combat Talent,Fencing Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_FENCING_TALENTS|1	DESC:The target suffers a -2 penalty to its armor class until the end of your next turn. For every 5 points of base attack bonus you possess, this penalty increases by 1. Automation is partial; consult docs/sphere-catalog.md. Unautomated rules must be applied manually.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/fencing#toc37
